# Bonsai · Git LFS tracking
# Founder ruling B-2 · APPROVED 12 September 2026:
#   "Track the large visual/canonical binary assets through Git LFS before
#    their first committed introduction."
#
# Timing is the whole point. Git does not forget: a binary committed as a plain
# blob stays in history for every future clone, and moving it to LFS afterwards
# requires a history rewrite. At the time this file was written only 2.9 MB of
# binaries existed in history and 79.7 MB were still uncommitted — so every
# pattern below must be in place BEFORE the canon intake commit lands.

# --- Canonical visual artifacts (W7 approved visual package) ---
*.png   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpeg  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webp  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.gif   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# --- Sender packages retained for provenance (docs/99-archive/) ---
*.zip   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pdf   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# --- Fonts, if any are ever vendored rather than loaded from a CDN ---
*.woff  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.woff2 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# --- Line-ending hygiene for text the project itself owns ---
# Deliberately scoped to source, NOT applied repository-wide. See the canon
# exemption below for why a blanket *.csv / *.md rule is unsafe here.
src/**          text eol=lf
messages/*.json text eol=lf
supabase/**     text eol=lf
*.ts            text eol=lf
*.tsx           text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf

# --- Canon and archive: byte-exact, never normalized ---
# These trees are verified against sender SHA-256 manifests. Line-ending
# normalization would rewrite bytes and permanently break that verification --
# six W2/W3/W4 evidence CSVs genuinely contain CRLF and are listed in
# 05-workstreams/W2-.../SHA256SUMS.txt and its siblings. `-text` disables
# all eol conversion so `shasum -a 256 -c` keeps passing for the life of the
# repository. Integrity of received authority outranks diff tidiness.
docs/01-canon/**    -text
docs/99-archive/**  -text
